1
00:00:08,520 --> 00:00:11,120
Well, turn on the lights and take a step back,
will you?

2
00:00:38,520 --> 00:00:42,920
It'll all work out eventually.

3
00:00:55,960 --> 00:00:59,920
Anyone without a job, come to my place.

4
00:00:59,920 --> 00:01:04,520
I don't have one either, so don't worry.

5
00:01:04,520 --> 00:01:11,960
Look, even Akaneru is on fire.

6
00:01:13,500 --> 00:01:18,260
It'll all work out somehow.

7
00:01:20,360 --> 00:01:23,520
You get it, right? Got it, got it.

8
00:01:23,520 --> 00:01:27,460
Once you understand,
gather round and follow me.

9
00:01:41,180 --> 00:01:44,800
Shrimp, crab,
squid: giant bio-creatures attack!

10
00:01:46,440 --> 00:01:47,160
What is this?

11
00:01:48,460 --> 00:01:49,980
What's wrong, senpai?

12
00:01:49,980 --> 00:01:52,740
What do you mean,
"what's wrong"? Look at this!

13
00:01:54,860 --> 00:01:57,160
The shrimp place at the bento
shop in front of the station,

14
00:01:57,160 --> 00:01:59,620
look closely.
Can you really call this a shrimp place?

15
00:02:01,360 --> 00:02:04,400
What are you talking about?
That's a perfectly good shrimp tempura!

16
00:02:05,160 --> 00:02:08,500
Look again.
This isn't a shrimp tempura bowl,

17
00:02:08,500 --> 00:02:12,380
it's a bowl of tempura batter!
Small doesn't even begin to cover it!

18
00:02:16,440 --> 00:02:18,480
Yes, this is Kōen-mae Hashutsujo.

19
00:02:22,280 --> 00:02:23,760
What do you mean by that?

20
00:02:24,520 --> 00:02:26,160
What's wrong, Terai-san?

21
00:02:26,160 --> 00:02:28,540
We got a report that there was an accident.

22
00:02:29,620 --> 00:02:32,640
An accident?
Apparently a car slipped on a banana peel.

23
00:02:32,640 --> 00:02:42,160
A car slipped on a banana? This isn't some old slapstick cartoon!
Something that stupid can't really happen!

24
00:02:42,640 --> 00:02:44,140
We should be at the scene soon.

25
00:02:52,640 --> 00:02:55,120
There's no doubt about it,
that's a real banana peel.

26
00:02:55,120 --> 00:02:56,600
It's a bit too big, though.

27
00:02:56,600 --> 00:02:59,300
Why would something like this
be in the middle of the road?

28
00:03:00,420 --> 00:03:02,260
Who would've dropped it here?

29
00:03:02,260 --> 00:03:04,560
The banana just talked!

30
00:03:04,560 --> 00:03:05,880
A banana monster!

31
00:03:06,820 --> 00:03:09,960
That voice sounds familiar.

32
00:03:10,860 --> 00:03:13,180
Long time no see, Gorilla-kun.

33
00:03:13,180 --> 00:03:14,940
Professor Esaki.

34
00:03:14,940 --> 00:03:16,540
I knew it was you.

35
00:03:17,440 --> 00:03:19,400
Esaki Bio Research Institute.

36
00:03:19,960 --> 00:03:23,060
You went and built this shady
building without anyone noticing!

37
00:03:23,800 --> 00:03:26,660
Did you make that giant banana here too?

38
00:03:26,660 --> 00:03:30,560
I tried to throw it out as kitchen waste,
but it wouldn't fit in the garbage bag.

39
00:03:31,220 --> 00:03:33,540
I was going to take it straight
to the waste disposal plant...

40
00:03:33,540 --> 00:03:35,960
Apparently it fell off the car on the way.

41
00:03:35,960 --> 00:03:37,760
What a troublemaker.

42
00:03:39,100 --> 00:03:40,560
This one's amazing.

43
00:03:40,560 --> 00:03:42,940
They're all dozens of
times bigger than normal.

44
00:03:56,020 --> 00:03:59,140
I made it to prepare for
the coming food crisis.

45
00:03:59,140 --> 00:04:01,260
Is it one of those
genetically modified things?

46
00:04:01,260 --> 00:04:07,180
No! In my case, I've been steadily
breeding varieties for decades.

47
00:04:07,180 --> 00:04:10,160
Would you like to try some tasting,
Garira-ken?

48
00:04:10,160 --> 00:04:12,380
It's really safe, right?

49
00:04:12,380 --> 00:04:14,400
Of course it's safe, no problem.

50
00:04:14,840 --> 00:04:15,440
Probably.

51
00:04:15,440 --> 00:04:17,880
With you, that
"probably" is what worries me.

52
00:04:20,840 --> 00:04:23,700
Yes. I'll have to decline.

53
00:04:27,120 --> 00:04:29,440
First, here's the rice.

54
00:04:29,940 --> 00:04:30,420
What's this?

55
00:04:30,960 --> 00:04:34,300
Here is Giant Koshihikari No. 28.

56
00:04:34,920 --> 00:04:38,900
One grain is about five bowls of rice.
What's the side dish?

57
00:04:39,120 --> 00:04:39,740
I'm back.

58
00:04:43,620 --> 00:04:44,980
Here's the natto.

59
00:04:46,060 --> 00:04:46,860
Natto?

60
00:04:47,200 --> 00:04:49,300
Please pour it over the rice and enjoy.

61
00:04:51,460 --> 00:04:53,520
It's just sitting on top, you know.

62
00:04:54,020 --> 00:04:55,660
Here's the cow soup.

63
00:04:56,460 --> 00:04:58,300
Here's the kawari daikon.

64
00:04:58,300 --> 00:05:00,740
Let's just eat whatever
we can and head home.

65
00:05:00,740 --> 00:05:01,940
How many minutes?

66
00:05:06,220 --> 00:05:08,220
How does it taste?

67
00:05:08,220 --> 00:05:11,580
It's not bad, but it's definitely
a bit coarse in flavor, isn't it?

68
00:05:12,280 --> 00:05:12,720
I see.

69
00:05:13,380 --> 00:05:16,020
Not bad, but coarse.

70
00:05:16,020 --> 00:05:17,240
What are you writing?

71
00:05:17,240 --> 00:05:18,000
Let me out of there!

72
00:05:18,000 --> 00:05:18,540
Don't look!

73
00:05:18,540 --> 00:05:19,940
- Everyone together!
- What is it? What is it?

74
00:05:20,180 --> 00:05:21,720
This is...

75
00:05:22,240 --> 00:05:25,360
So you really were conducting human experiments on your senior's body,
weren't you?

76
00:05:25,360 --> 00:05:27,960
Hey! What on earth is going on here?

77
00:05:28,180 --> 00:05:28,565
No, well,

78
00:05:28,615 --> 00:05:33,120
Gorilla-kun's special body won't
budge for something like this, so

79
00:05:33,120 --> 00:05:33,860
Don't you dare joke around!

80
00:05:34,040 --> 00:05:36,040
- No, Nakagawa, we're going home!
- Then, bye!

81
00:05:36,600 --> 00:05:37,340
Wait!

82
00:05:37,660 --> 00:05:41,760
People with special bodies like
Gorilla-kun are hard to find.

83
00:05:41,760 --> 00:05:43,640
Stay with me just a little longer.

84
00:05:43,640 --> 00:05:45,360
- No way!
- Of course, for humans!

85
00:05:45,360 --> 00:05:48,440
I won't say it's free, I'll pay you
part-time wages in cash, you know.

86
00:05:48,440 --> 00:05:50,180
Part-time pay, in cash.

87
00:05:50,740 --> 00:05:53,120
Actually, this future food crisis...

88
00:05:53,120 --> 00:05:55,920
is something I've been
worried about for a long time.

89
00:05:56,300 --> 00:05:57,980
It's for the future of humanity.

90
00:05:57,980 --> 00:06:00,800
If it's me, I'd be happy to help.

91
00:06:00,800 --> 00:06:01,920
Will you do it?

92
00:06:02,800 --> 00:06:04,840
The seeds are huge, so it's hard to eat.

93
00:06:05,280 --> 00:06:07,220
The skin is thick and hard to peel.

94
00:06:07,220 --> 00:06:09,320
It's lacking bitterness,
the bitterness is lacking.

95
00:06:09,760 --> 00:06:11,200
Katsuobushi, how about it?

96
00:06:11,900 --> 00:06:13,360
Blue bonito flakes, how about it?

97
00:06:15,360 --> 00:06:17,240
Are you already full, senpai?

98
00:06:17,360 --> 00:06:19,820
Vegetables and fruit only get boring

99
00:06:20,360 --> 00:06:21,760
Is there no meat? Where's the meat!

100
00:06:22,100 --> 00:06:23,780
Of course, we've prepared some.

101
00:06:24,240 --> 00:06:24,800
Haah...

102
00:06:27,320 --> 00:06:28,060
Here it is.

103
00:06:31,360 --> 00:06:32,700
W-what on earth is that?

104
00:06:38,620 --> 00:06:39,800
Gorilla-kun

105
00:06:42,280 --> 00:06:43,000
He's gone.

106
00:06:43,000 --> 00:06:44,400
Over here, over here!

107
00:06:49,300 --> 00:06:52,020
He's gone and turned into a flat gorilla!

108
00:06:54,340 --> 00:06:55,620
No way I'm becoming that!

109
00:06:55,620 --> 00:06:57,880
What is this thing?

110
00:06:57,880 --> 00:07:00,380
That's Pyonkichi, the giant frog.

111
00:07:00,380 --> 00:07:01,540
Pyonkichi

112
00:07:02,700 --> 00:07:04,060
It's Pyonkichi!

113
00:07:04,780 --> 00:07:06,380
Are we going to eat this one too?

114
00:07:07,060 --> 00:07:08,540
No, he's a pet.

115
00:07:08,540 --> 00:07:09,460
A pet?

116
00:07:10,340 --> 00:07:14,540
Yes, my research isn't only about the food crisis,
you know.

117
00:07:14,540 --> 00:07:18,780
Look at what's happening on Earth right now,
in 2002.

118
00:07:19,380 --> 00:07:21,280
Rice paddies keep disappearing,

119
00:07:21,280 --> 00:07:24,380
and the little greenery
left is exposed to acid.

120
00:07:24,380 --> 00:07:27,440
Rising CO2 is destroying the ozone layer.

121
00:07:27,440 --> 00:07:28,880
Ultraviolet rays pour down.

122
00:07:28,880 --> 00:07:30,220
Temperatures keep rising.

123
00:07:30,220 --> 00:07:34,220
Because of these factors,
the number of frogs is plummeting.

124
00:07:34,220 --> 00:07:38,260
So I created a frog strong and
sturdy enough to beat anything,

125
00:07:38,260 --> 00:07:41,980
a true King of Frogs.
That's what I set out to make.

126
00:07:42,920 --> 00:07:44,220
So this is the one?

127
00:07:45,120 --> 00:07:46,960
Stop it, stop it!

128
00:07:46,960 --> 00:07:49,320
Looks like Hyonkichi
has taken a liking to him.

129
00:07:49,320 --> 00:07:49,780
What?

130
00:07:50,480 --> 00:07:53,380
Normally he catches flies
and things under there.

131
00:07:53,380 --> 00:07:54,820
Well, don't worry about it.

132
00:07:54,820 --> 00:07:55,960
Don't worry about it, he says?

133
00:07:58,740 --> 00:08:00,260
What's inside?

134
00:08:01,880 --> 00:08:03,100
What is this thing?

135
00:08:03,100 --> 00:08:04,280
It's whitebait.

136
00:08:04,280 --> 00:08:04,900
What?

137
00:08:04,900 --> 00:08:06,880
Looking closely, it really is

138
00:08:06,880 --> 00:08:09,920
but when it's this big,
it doesn't feel like whitebait anymore.

139
00:08:10,420 --> 00:08:11,460
It's a clam.

140
00:08:11,460 --> 00:08:14,080
Looks like a person might come out of it.

141
00:08:14,960 --> 00:08:15,820
It's sea urchin.

142
00:08:16,400 --> 00:08:17,140
What spines!

143
00:08:17,140 --> 00:08:19,220
It's going to be a pain to catch.

144
00:08:19,940 --> 00:08:20,740
That one...

145
00:08:28,420 --> 00:08:30,820
Whoa, isn't that a spiny lobster?

146
00:08:30,820 --> 00:08:34,440
If we made tempura out of that one,
it'd be incredibly filling.

147
00:08:35,580 --> 00:08:37,420
Alright, that spiny lobster first.

148
00:08:37,420 --> 00:08:38,940
We're turning that one into tempura.

149
00:08:40,340 --> 00:08:41,440
Alright, got it.

150
00:08:58,880 --> 00:09:01,680
-Let's go!-Let's go!

151
00:09:23,520 --> 00:09:24,640
Thanks for the save, Kankichi!

152
00:09:25,020 --> 00:09:25,340
Thank you!

153
00:09:29,280 --> 00:09:30,740
My aquarium!

154
00:09:39,600 --> 00:09:41,020
Hey, you two!

155
00:09:42,300 --> 00:09:43,580
Three of them are heading outside!

156
00:09:44,600 --> 00:09:47,200
If they get out into town like this,
it'll be a disaster!

157
00:09:47,580 --> 00:09:49,600
Don't let them get away! My shrimp tempura!

158
00:10:03,000 --> 00:10:05,720
Your father's special
effects really are the best.

159
00:10:06,160 --> 00:10:07,240
This stuff is old-fashioned.

160
00:10:07,240 --> 00:10:09,300
We're in the age of CG now.

161
00:10:09,300 --> 00:10:11,600
Something that bursts
right out of the screen,

162
00:10:11,600 --> 00:10:13,680
we have to create visuals with real impact.

163
00:10:24,080 --> 00:10:25,480
They really did jump out!

164
00:10:25,480 --> 00:10:26,660
What a force!

165
00:10:36,620 --> 00:10:38,580
Yes, this is Kameari Park police box.

166
00:10:42,220 --> 00:10:43,620
What do you mean by that?

167
00:10:43,920 --> 00:10:44,720
What's wrong?

168
00:10:45,200 --> 00:10:49,180
Giant shrimp, crabs,
and squid are rampaging through the streets!

169
00:10:49,640 --> 00:10:51,360
Isn't this a prank call?

170
00:10:53,220 --> 00:10:54,020
It's serious!

171
00:10:54,440 --> 00:10:55,780
What happened, Kei-chan?

172
00:10:56,300 --> 00:11:00,100
Professor Esaki's giant
bio-creatures have escaped into town!

173
00:11:00,640 --> 00:11:02,300
Giant bio-creatures!

174
00:11:02,300 --> 00:11:04,420
Hurry, Pyonkichi!

175
00:11:06,160 --> 00:11:08,320
Don't let the leader get away!

176
00:11:09,500 --> 00:11:11,060
It's a prank call.

177
00:11:11,480 --> 00:11:12,900
So it wasn't a prank after all

178
00:11:12,900 --> 00:11:14,840
What a big spiny lobster!

179
00:11:15,280 --> 00:11:17,980
Lobsters this size rarely come in, you know.

180
00:11:17,980 --> 00:11:18,820
How about it?

181
00:11:18,820 --> 00:11:19,780
That one.

182
00:11:20,680 --> 00:11:23,080
Aaaaaah!

183
00:11:29,100 --> 00:11:31,180
Whoa, this one's a big catch!

184
00:11:31,180 --> 00:11:32,820
Aaaaaah!

185
00:11:35,700 --> 00:11:37,580
When did it turn into two of them?

186
00:11:37,580 --> 00:11:38,740
But what could it be?

187
00:11:38,740 --> 00:11:40,720
What is it?

188
00:11:46,480 --> 00:11:49,300
The giant creatures are
reportedly missing near Shimahada.

189
00:11:49,720 --> 00:11:51,220
Something that big...

190
00:11:51,940 --> 00:11:53,760
Where could it have hidden?

191
00:11:59,720 --> 00:12:03,700
The giant creatures are heading
toward Asakusa at quite a speed.

192
00:12:04,640 --> 00:12:09,200
This? Didn't I put tracking devices on the
creatures in case something like this happened?

193
00:12:09,200 --> 00:12:11,860
You should have told us that sooner.

194
00:12:12,480 --> 00:12:16,820
Senpai! It's Asakusa!
The giant creatures are heading for Asakusa!

195
00:12:17,040 --> 00:12:17,540
Asakusa!

196
00:12:19,600 --> 00:12:22,160
Next stop, Asakusa, Asakusa.

197
00:12:22,700 --> 00:12:29,780
Hurry up! Tendon! Tendon!

198
00:12:34,580 --> 00:12:36,220
Japan, this is the country

199
00:12:44,980 --> 00:12:52,760
Ladies and gentlemen, please look. One of Japan's proud tourist
landmarks is about to be destroyed by mysterious giant creatures.

200
00:12:53,220 --> 00:13:00,120
The giant creatures have destroyed Kaminarimon and are
currently advancing along Nakamise-dori toward Sensō-ji.

201
00:13:00,120 --> 00:13:01,380
Aaah, that's...

202
00:13:01,380 --> 00:13:04,800
Dammit! They're running
wild like they own the place!

203
00:13:16,240 --> 00:13:18,420
How dare you, mere tempura ingredients!

204
00:13:19,020 --> 00:13:20,200
Go, Pyonkichi!

205
00:13:23,420 --> 00:13:25,100
Final Tempura!

206
00:13:31,660 --> 00:13:35,465
The giant tree frog charged at the three giant creatures,
but

207
00:13:35,515 --> 00:13:37,740
it's completely helpless against them.

208
00:13:38,860 --> 00:14:00,520
Nooooooooooooooooooooo!

209
00:14:00,520 --> 00:14:02,240
He got knocked away!

210
00:14:02,240 --> 00:14:03,680
That's...

211
00:14:05,160 --> 00:14:07,500
Operation Ultra Tempura!

212
00:14:07,500 --> 00:14:08,200
That's it!

213
00:14:08,200 --> 00:14:10,160
Listen, here's the plan.

214
00:14:14,120 --> 00:14:16,200
Traffic is blocked beyond this point.

215
00:14:16,920 --> 00:14:18,440
At the Komagabashi intersection,

216
00:14:18,440 --> 00:14:20,380
the police have set up

217
00:14:20,380 --> 00:14:21,240
a giant pot.

218
00:14:21,240 --> 00:14:24,020
What's going to happen now?

219
00:14:29,560 --> 00:14:31,120
The oil level is OK!

220
00:14:31,120 --> 00:14:32,560
Alright, ignition!

221
00:14:36,320 --> 00:14:40,060
The oil poured into the giant pot
is being heated with a flamethrower.

222
00:14:40,060 --> 00:14:43,320
Don't tell me they're actually
planning to deep-fry tempura?

223
00:14:48,160 --> 00:14:50,180
Alright, our side is ready too.

224
00:14:50,680 --> 00:14:52,160
Okay, let's go, Pyonkichi!

225
00:14:54,020 --> 00:14:57,600
The giant creatures are currently heading south down Kokusai-dori!
Heading south down Kokusai-dori!

226
00:15:01,080 --> 00:15:04,080
Hey, hey, you guys! It's feeding time!

227
00:15:07,680 --> 00:15:10,038
The giant creatures are now being

228
00:15:10,088 --> 00:15:13,400
lured from Kokusai-dori onto
Asakusa-dori by the giant frog!

229
00:15:13,840 --> 00:15:14,700
Hey, hey!

230
00:15:36,300 --> 00:15:39,660
Thrash about, thrash about, the more you thrash,
the better the batter sticks.

231
00:15:42,580 --> 00:15:44,700
The three of them are coating
themselves in tempura batter as they go.

232
00:15:44,700 --> 00:15:47,180
They're being lured toward Komagata Bridge.

233
00:16:08,380 --> 00:16:09,640
We did it! We really did it!

234
00:16:09,640 --> 00:16:13,300
The giant creatures are fried
to a nice golden-brown tempura.

235
00:16:13,300 --> 00:16:16,100
Tokyo's crisis has now vanished.

236
00:16:16,520 --> 00:16:18,880
I don't think that was the last one.

237
00:16:18,880 --> 00:16:22,280
If we keep forgetting
to coexist with nature,

238
00:16:24,020 --> 00:16:26,340
as long as we do,
a second and third incident will happen.

239
00:16:26,340 --> 00:16:28,780
That one wasn't the last one.

240
00:16:28,780 --> 00:16:31,300
You've got plenty of them at your place,
haven't you?

241
00:16:32,820 --> 00:16:36,220
Well, all that's left is to cook the
rice and make it into tempura bowls.

242
00:16:36,220 --> 00:16:38,980
I'll let you have some too, Hyonkichi.

243
00:16:40,520 --> 00:16:41,900
What's wrong, Hyonkichi?

244
00:16:42,320 --> 00:16:43,400
I wonder if he's tired.

245
00:16:44,100 --> 00:16:44,960
Maybe he's sleepy.

246
00:16:45,400 --> 00:16:47,860
It's normally hibernation season for frogs,
after all.

247
00:16:48,480 --> 00:16:49,200
I see.

248
00:16:49,200 --> 00:16:53,260
When you wake from hibernation, I'll
feed you plenty of your favorite things.

249
00:16:54,020 --> 00:16:54,580
Go to sleep.

250
00:16:58,300 --> 00:16:59,840
Wow, amazing!

251
00:17:00,280 --> 00:17:01,520
Well then, let's get started.

252
00:17:01,520 --> 00:17:03,060
Let's eat!

253
00:17:08,380 --> 00:17:09,180
Delicious.

254
00:17:09,720 --> 00:17:12,180
I've never had a tempura
bowl this delicious before.

255
00:17:12,180 --> 00:17:14,240
And the meat is packed in tight too.

256
00:17:14,240 --> 00:17:17,640
It's the fruit of years of research.

257
00:17:18,120 --> 00:17:19,420
By the way, where's Ryo-chan?

258
00:17:19,680 --> 00:17:21,500
He was the one who
wanted to eat it the most.

259
00:17:22,520 --> 00:17:25,980
H-hey! Let me go!

260
00:17:26,400 --> 00:17:31,060
Why do I have to hibernate with you?!
Let me go!

261
00:17:32,340 --> 00:17:38,400
N-no way, he's planning to make me
his food during hibernation! Help!

262
00:17:40,480 --> 00:17:44,280
Is this the apartment? The one where
the residents are having a huge fight?

263
00:17:44,280 --> 00:17:46,940
Yes, please do something about it.

264
00:17:46,940 --> 00:17:50,340
They're at odds over each room's hobbies.

265
00:17:51,500 --> 00:17:52,560
I don't really get it.

266
00:17:54,580 --> 00:17:57,180
Anyway, just hear me out.

267
00:17:57,180 --> 00:17:58,080
Yeah, sure.

268
00:17:59,380 --> 00:18:01,700
Mr. Akai, Mr. Owari has come
to hear what you have to say.

269
00:18:02,180 --> 00:18:03,040
That's fine.

270
00:18:03,740 --> 00:18:04,100
This is...

271
00:18:05,220 --> 00:18:06,740
Please, come in.

272
00:18:07,400 --> 00:18:10,140
Wow, you really went all in on red,
didn't you?

273
00:18:10,840 --> 00:18:11,980
Please, help yourself if you like.

274
00:18:11,980 --> 00:18:15,540
Strawberries and cherries with ketchup,
and tomato juice.

275
00:18:16,740 --> 00:18:19,580
Until last month,
I worked at the post office, but...

276
00:18:21,500 --> 00:18:28,060
Your eyes look bloodshot. I work a lot of night shifts because of my job,
but being surrounded by all this red...

277
00:18:28,060 --> 00:18:33,480
It's a job worth living for. That beautiful red,
the guy in 602 insults it.

278
00:18:34,060 --> 00:18:40,180
Well, everyone has different favorite colors.
What are you saying? Even you, Officer?

279
00:18:40,180 --> 00:18:45,780
What color is your home? Red, right?
Red is the source of human life.

280
00:18:45,780 --> 00:18:48,260
Shall I show you?

281
00:18:48,260 --> 00:18:52,720
Got it. Red is wonderful.
I'll go talk him around.

282
00:18:52,720 --> 00:18:54,960
Then I'm counting on you.

283
00:18:54,960 --> 00:18:59,200
Got it, got it.
What a man of strong principles.

284
00:18:59,200 --> 00:19:01,000
That's exactly why it's such a problem.

285
00:19:04,400 --> 00:19:07,480
Ms. Midorikawa,
the officers have come to hear your story.

286
00:19:07,480 --> 00:19:09,100
I see. Please, go ahead.

287
00:19:09,100 --> 00:19:12,080
Good grief, this place is like a jungle!

288
00:19:12,080 --> 00:19:14,860
What on earth are you doing?

289
00:19:15,780 --> 00:19:16,340
It's nothing, really.

290
00:19:17,400 --> 00:19:20,740
You know that green is the best color for human eyes,
don't you?

291
00:19:20,740 --> 00:19:24,940
Not just the eyes,
green is an important friend to people.

292
00:19:24,940 --> 00:19:25,880
But,

293
00:19:25,880 --> 00:19:27,300
red is bad for the eyes.

294
00:19:27,300 --> 00:19:29,480
As the saying goes,
"Associate with vermilion and you'll turn red."

295
00:19:29,480 --> 00:19:31,140
It's a color that corrupts you.

296
00:19:31,140 --> 00:19:33,160
For people to change naturally,

297
00:19:33,160 --> 00:19:35,920
green is an essential color.

298
00:19:35,920 --> 00:19:38,200
I've pretty much understood
the situation now,

299
00:19:39,060 --> 00:19:41,860
so let's sit down and talk
slowly over some salad next time.

300
00:19:42,540 --> 00:19:43,760
Yeah, well then, see you later.

301
00:19:45,780 --> 00:19:48,180
Next up is Mr. Kimoto in 607.

302
00:19:48,740 --> 00:19:50,300
It's open, come on in.

303
00:19:50,300 --> 00:19:52,480
Whoa, what is this?

304
00:19:53,620 --> 00:19:56,020
The clash of the two
colors is hurting my eyes.

305
00:19:56,820 --> 00:19:57,620
Are you all right?

306
00:19:58,860 --> 00:20:00,400
Okay, it's fine now.

307
00:20:00,920 --> 00:20:02,440
Listen to me, officer.

308
00:20:02,880 --> 00:20:04,920
The people on this floor are a nuisance.

309
00:20:04,920 --> 00:20:08,020
They even painted the inside of
their homes in that tacky color.

310
00:20:08,020 --> 00:20:09,200
Are you out of your mind?

311
00:20:09,200 --> 00:20:11,520
But this place is bright yellow too,
isn't it?

312
00:20:12,040 --> 00:20:14,280
A fortune said yellow was my lucky color.

313
00:20:14,280 --> 00:20:15,220
Sorry.

314
00:20:15,780 --> 00:20:17,560
Honestly, they're all such odd ones.

315
00:20:17,560 --> 00:20:19,040
Next up is a doctor.

316
00:20:19,040 --> 00:20:20,480
This one seems more normal.

317
00:20:21,980 --> 00:20:23,580
Is Mr. Shirayama here?

318
00:20:24,980 --> 00:20:26,280
We've been waiting for you.

319
00:20:27,560 --> 00:20:30,060
Given my line of work,
white is the most calming color.

320
00:20:31,160 --> 00:20:33,060
Well, would you care for some milk?

321
00:20:33,060 --> 00:20:37,280
It's a frightening room. One wrong step
and it would look like an unfinished job.

322
00:20:37,280 --> 00:20:40,000
Modern people are all being overrun by color,
aren't they.

323
00:20:40,000 --> 00:20:44,280
To heal from all that, white is the best,
since it lets you empty your mind.

324
00:20:45,780 --> 00:20:47,400
The conflict here is intense.

325
00:20:47,400 --> 00:20:49,640
That's why there are so many fights.

326
00:20:51,520 --> 00:20:53,420
Mr. Kanada, are you going out?

327
00:20:54,820 --> 00:20:56,040
Just going for a little walk.

328
00:20:56,500 --> 00:20:58,820
Who's that gaudy, gold-plated guy?

329
00:20:58,820 --> 00:21:01,260
That's Mr. Kanada from Room 610.

330
00:21:01,260 --> 00:21:03,120
He doesn't pick fights.

331
00:21:03,120 --> 00:21:05,120
They say the rich don't quarrel.

332
00:21:05,120 --> 00:21:07,420
Isn't he going to get kidnapped like that?

333
00:21:09,040 --> 00:21:09,720
Please, come in.

334
00:21:10,640 --> 00:21:12,780
And last is Mr. Kurobara, the pastor.

335
00:21:12,780 --> 00:21:15,820
I thought there'd be a doctor,
but there's a pastor too?

336
00:21:16,300 --> 00:21:17,280
Excuse us.

337
00:21:17,280 --> 00:21:19,400
It's pitch-black in here!

338
00:21:20,560 --> 00:21:22,620
Hey, Pastor, where are you?

339
00:21:23,160 --> 00:21:23,960
Over here.

340
00:21:25,140 --> 00:21:27,400
Don't scare us like that.
At least turn on the light.

341
00:21:27,400 --> 00:21:28,260
It's on.

342
00:21:28,260 --> 00:21:31,840
Everything in the room is black,
so it's just hard to see.

343
00:21:32,580 --> 00:21:34,220
Step outside for a moment.

344
00:21:34,820 --> 00:21:35,760
See?

345
00:21:36,280 --> 00:21:39,560
He's painted his face, his shoes,
and even blackened his teeth.

346
00:21:40,280 --> 00:21:41,820
Black is a sacred color.

347
00:21:42,780 --> 00:21:44,660
Mourning clothes are all black, right?

348
00:21:45,060 --> 00:21:48,140
If you pour coffee into a black cup,
you can't tell how much is in it, right?

349
00:21:48,860 --> 00:21:50,080
Milk and sugar?

350
00:21:50,180 --> 00:21:52,080
We have no milk, but there's sugar.

351
00:21:52,660 --> 00:21:53,840
Yes, black sugar.

352
00:21:53,840 --> 00:21:54,860
I thought so.

353
00:21:54,860 --> 00:21:57,520
What's that sound?

354
00:21:57,780 --> 00:21:58,980
That's our pet.

355
00:21:58,980 --> 00:22:00,700
A pitch-black black leopard.

356
00:22:02,340 --> 00:22:03,480
Where's the exit?

357
00:22:03,540 --> 00:22:05,260
Hey, Boxy, don't close your eyes!

358
00:22:05,260 --> 00:22:06,940
We can't tell where anyone is.

359
00:22:10,480 --> 00:22:12,820
This apartment building is a mess!

360
00:22:12,820 --> 00:22:16,100
That's why I'm asking you to do something about it,
aren't I?

361
00:22:16,100 --> 00:22:17,140
What did you say?

362
00:22:17,140 --> 00:22:19,180
Here we go again.

363
00:22:19,180 --> 00:22:22,100
You people have no sense
of color at all, do you?

364
00:22:22,100 --> 00:22:24,080
Shut up, you're the one!

365
00:22:24,080 --> 00:22:25,140
What did you just say?

366
00:22:25,140 --> 00:22:27,080
That's it, I've had enough!

367
00:22:28,080 --> 00:22:30,000
Don't look at me,
I have nothing to do with this.

368
00:22:30,000 --> 00:22:31,700
You're all the same.

369
00:22:32,940 --> 00:22:36,140
Your poverty of spirit is caused by your good looks,
you know.

370
00:22:36,140 --> 00:22:38,400
I'll give you money, so make up already.

371
00:22:39,840 --> 00:22:40,740
You idiot!

372
00:22:40,920 --> 00:22:42,940
Even rich people get
angry when they have to!

373
00:22:43,280 --> 00:22:44,580
Stop it!

374
00:22:44,800 --> 00:22:45,460
Damn it!

375
00:22:45,600 --> 00:22:47,020
I'll tear everything to pieces!

376
00:22:47,480 --> 00:22:49,620
That's why we need more green!

377
00:22:51,920 --> 00:22:53,820
Stop it! Do as I say!

378
00:22:53,820 --> 00:22:54,920
Stop it!

379
00:23:00,500 --> 00:23:01,720
The colors are gone?

380
00:23:01,880 --> 00:23:03,260
My money...

381
00:23:03,260 --> 00:23:04,740
It's turned black and white.

382
00:23:05,260 --> 00:23:10,500
Look, we've been obsessing over color so much that God got
angry and turned everything into a black-and-white cartoon!

383
00:23:11,380 --> 00:23:11,740
No way.

384
00:23:12,340 --> 00:23:13,500
What are we going to do

385
00:23:13,500 --> 00:23:14,680
now?

386
00:23:15,140 --> 00:23:17,040
Don't worry about it.

387
00:23:17,040 --> 00:23:20,360
When we were kids,
all TVs were black and white.

388
00:23:20,360 --> 00:23:22,820
But everyone still happily watched them.

389
00:23:22,820 --> 00:23:24,940
But look at TV these days.

390
00:23:24,940 --> 00:23:27,620
Color, stereo, digital, high-definition...

391
00:23:27,620 --> 00:23:30,940
Technology keeps advancing,
but the content hasn't kept up.

392
00:23:30,940 --> 00:23:34,800
As long as the content is interesting,
you don't need color!

393
00:23:35,320 --> 00:23:37,600
That's right, we don't need colors at all.

394
00:23:37,600 --> 00:23:39,820
We were wrong.

395
00:23:40,280 --> 00:23:41,440
Yes, that's right, everyone.

396
00:23:42,560 --> 00:23:44,380
Let us give thanks to God.

397
00:23:44,380 --> 00:23:47,300
Something that doesn't change even
when it's turned black and white.

398
00:23:47,300 --> 00:23:49,840
Officer, we were the ones at fault.

399
00:23:49,840 --> 00:23:51,760
Did you understand, you two?

400
00:23:52,680 --> 00:23:53,880
Look!

401
00:23:53,880 --> 00:23:57,560
That beautiful rainbow,
worthy of a happy ending!

402
00:23:57,560 --> 00:24:00,220
It just doesn't quite click, does it.

403
00:24:00,940 --> 00:24:02,100
I don't really get it, it's like an anime.

404
00:24:02,100 --> 00:24:03,500
No, it has to be in color!

405
00:24:44,940 --> 00:24:48,260
Next time

406
00:25:02,600 --> 00:25:04,160
With this kind of spirit

407
00:25:04,160 --> 00:25:07,640
What's hard to understand

408
00:25:08,660 --> 00:25:11,460
is that we want to look that way.

409
00:25:12,400 --> 00:25:17,220
Isn't that better than being all show?

410
00:25:18,900 --> 00:25:21,060
Nanana

411
00:25:21,060 --> 00:25:22,460
Nanana

412
00:25:23,100 --> 00:25:23,520
Nanana

413
00:25:29,460 --> 00:25:31,140
Oh no!

414
00:25:32,600 --> 00:25:34,900
We've lost the Chief's
wedding ring somewhere!

415
00:25:34,900 --> 00:25:38,540
It must have gotten mixed into
the teddy bear Reiko was making!

416
00:25:38,540 --> 00:25:40,760
We sold 200 of them at the bazaar?

417
00:25:41,000 --> 00:25:43,880
In that case, we've got no choice
but to check every single one!

418
00:25:43,880 --> 00:25:46,800
Next time: Search high and low!
A great pursuit!

419
00:25:46,800 --> 00:25:47,880
See you then!

420
00:25:48,800 --> 00:25:50,960
Over there, it's Kameari.

421
00:25:52,060 --> 00:25:54,680
Well, it's probably Kameari.

422
00:25:55,740 --> 00:25:59,360
Everyone, come on over to our town!

423
00:26:00,520 --> 00:26:00,880
Thank you.

424
00:26:02,600 --> 00:26:03,820
Thank you for watching.

